// Act II: the summons, Truth Pong, the Trust Chart, the printer (spec §3 D2–D8).
//
// Every beat here is a PUBLIC set piece: no subject is bound, so every
// line lands in the Desktop room for everyone. The state, timers and cues
// live in the story rules in main.loom that divert here; these beats are
// what the room reads. Names in the ranking beats come from Night.* vars
// the ROLE ranking watchers set before `rankings_done` fires.
//
// No line here may start `VLC:` / `MS Paint:` (a featured program never
// speaks, spec §0 rule 5): VLC and MS Paint get their printer nudges in
// their own DMs from main.loom's ROLE watchers.

== Five Minute Warning
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

// DRAFT w59 (in-world room name)
Every phone in the house buzzes at once. Five minutes. Somewhere in the Tube an Antivirus starts counting.
Clippy: Programs! Programs, it is time! Back to the Desktop for the Second Moment Of Truth! Five minutes!
// w26 (G1: the exemption is never said up front)
Clippy: And if you are not here— well. Please just be here.
// w18 (B10): the programs check themselves in.
Clippy: When you get here, scan the check-in sign by the door! That's your check-in. You can do it yourself! I believe in you!

== Summons Closed
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

The doors of the Desktop close.
Anyone who is not here, and is not in Bathroom Mode, is late. The Antivirus have the list.
Clippy: Okay. Okay! Everyone who is here is wonderful. Let's begin.

== Truth Pong
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Adobe Acrobat
  aloud: Clippy, Adobe Acrobat

Clippy is visibly distraught. Behind the tears, she is trying to be more excited than ever.
Clippy (through tears): It's Truth Time again! And this time we are going to reveal our truths in a fun new way. With a game of TRUTH PONG. Everyone's favourite game!
Clippy: Out in the Cloud there is a pyramid of cups on a folding table. We are all going to show that we are functional programs who can be trusted to retrieve truths accurately.
Clippy: By following one simple command. Bounce or throw a ping pong ball into a cup. We should all be able to do this, because we are being commanded to.
Clippy: If you miss, you will not be trusted to deliver a truth, and you will need to be reinstalled in the Internet.
// w26 (G1: the judging rule is never said out loud)
Clippy: If you make the cup, you get to share one truth, and every fact you filed with Trabolta this round counts. No cup, no count!
Adobe Acrobat: Visualise the cup. Become the cup. Then throw the ball into the cup.
Clippy: Everyone outside! Line up! It's going to be so fun!

// Wave 59a: TRABOLTA 5 to "Before we get to the answers for Round 2." He reads
// them on 🤖 now (Overshare Answers).
== Round Two Tally
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: Welcome back, programs.
Trabolta: What a fine round of Truth Pong. Jean Trabolta's Truth Scavenger Hunt is a finely tuned game. It's automatic. It's systematic. And once we get to Truth Pong, it is also hydromatic. It was fun to see you all get splashed with the beer or water and I wish I could be there with you in person, but circumstances do not allow.
Trabolta: Now.
Trabolta: Before we get to the answers for Round 2.

== Trust Chart
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta, Clippy

Trabolta: It is time for Trabolta's Trust Chart.
Trabolta: I have been monitoring your patterns and behaviours, as part of the beta testing terms of agreement you signed up for during onboarding, and I have some opinions on who I trust.
Clippy: Isn't this exciting? Somebody's going to be the most trusted program in the whole computer!

// Wave 59a: three from each end (main.loom's ranking machinery); a line with
// nobody in it drops out.
== Praise The Top
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: The program you should all respect the most as a trusted leader is: {Night.most_trusted}
if Night.second_trusted != "none":
  Trabolta: The program you should see as a deputy leader and trust as a primary leader in the event that the most trusted leader ever requires reinstallation is: {Night.second_trusted}
if Night.third_trusted != "none":
  Trabolta: A wildcard of sorts who you should consider trusting under certain circumstances is: {Night.third_trusted}

== Shame The Bottom
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: Now.
Trabolta: Trabolta's least trusted programs. These programs should be trusted like they are Scorpions.
if Night.third_least != "none":
  Trabolta: The third least trustworthy program, monitored closely, is: {Night.third_least}
if Night.second_least != "none":
  Trabolta: The second least trustworthy program, scrutinized intensely: {Night.second_least}
Trabolta: The most least trustworthy program, currently monitored for potential permanent reinstallation: {Night.least_trusted}

== Print The Certificate
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

// The Trust Chart stays on the screens (MOST / LEAST TRUSTED called out)
// through the praise, the shame and this ask; the certificate slide comes
// up only when someone presses START (The Printer Jams).
set Night.printer_called = true
if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "vlc" and p.cleared and not p.captured]) > 0:
  set Night.printer_vlc = true
Trabolta: Now that we have established trust.
Trabolta: It is time to print a Security Certificate PDF File for our most trusted program, {Night.most_trusted}. I cannot operate this function myself. Could someone please ensure the certificate is printed before we proceed.

== The Printer Jams
  setting: The Desktop

cue screens_print_certificate
set Night.screen = "print_certificate"
set Night.terminals = "print_certificate"
Someone presses START. The printer thinks about it. Nothing happens.
The screen says the certificate is printing. It has said that for a while.

== Full Of Beans
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Trabolta
  aloud: Clippy

Narrator: The printer is full of beans.
Clippy: Beans. Those are— those are symptoms. The malware is getting worse. Routine operations like print to PDF are no longer working. It is even more urgent that we get the next facts right.
// Wave 59a: TRABOLTA 6 PART 1.
Trabolta: This is a problem. A real problem.
Trabolta: There were not supposed to be any beans in the printer. This is a sign of significant entropy in the system.
Trabolta: Please, antiviruses. If there is anyone in the Internet, ZIP them up together and bring them out, forget the reinstallation. I need everyone here.

== Zip Everyone Out
  setting: The Desktop

The Antivirus march into the Internet and bring every program out of the Internet, one by one, zipped up and compressed for the moment.
Whatever was in there with them is still in there.
